resources.string:
Everything stays beautiful: season colours, gradients, artwork, smooth transitions and animations. Only what strains a weak phone changes:

• live decorations (shines, sparkles, gift and coin shimmer) are drawn at about 20 frames per second instead of 60;
• glass refreshes half as often, without the liquid-glass shimmer;
• chat photos load slightly smaller in a compact format - half the memory, no stutter while scrolling;
• the screen runs at the standard rate (no 90/120 Hz) - less heat;
• games show fewer particles and sparks, Rail Run has less side scenery and no heavy glows, in Durak live effects stay only on cards in your hand;
• animated emoji repeat fewer times, the shop coin burst is smaller.

Result: less heat, longer battery, smoother scrolling and games.

“Auto” turns it on by itself: on phones with little memory (under 3 GB), 4 CPU cores or fewer, or budget models; while the phone is badly overheating; and if the interface stutters noticeably (until the next launch).
